<DocsLayout title="Testing" description="Unit, scenario and blind pentest validation for the honeypot system" section="Testing" sidebar={sidebar} toc={toc}>
  <p>
    The testing strategy follows the architecture: pure rules can be proven without OpenResty, adapters are
   covered by scenario scripts against a running stack, and the blind pentest checks the whole thing from
    the outside. The suite is intentionally boring to run — a plain Lua interpreter and Python unittest.
  </p>

  <h2 id="layers">Testing Layers</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Unit / Integration Tests:</strong> Lua module logic, dashboard generation, timeline capture. Pure Lua modules (*_rules.lua) are testable under a plain Lua interpreter without OpenResty.</li>
    <li><strong>Functional Testing:</strong> End-to-end honeypot interaction and detection validation.</li>
    <li><strong>Blind Pentest Evaluation:</strong> Controlled adversary assessments with internal-test secret gating.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="coverage-map">Coverage Map</h2>
  <CardGrid columns={3}>
    <DocCard title="Pure rules" href="#unit" icon="code" tag="23 suites" description="Every *_rules.lua module has a matching test file covering positive matches, negatives and boundary values." meta="plain Lua" />
    <DocCard title="Scenario scripts" href="#running" icon="terminal" tag="9 scenarios" description="WooCommerce, OWASP WSTG, WPScan, Metasploit, hardening verification, database password replacement, payment gateway, backup deletion and PentAGI." meta="bash" />
    <DocCard title="Dashboard" href="#dashboard" icon="chart" tag="4 test files" description="NDJSON integrity, host settings, overview statistics and learning-page validation." meta="unittest" />
    <DocCard title="Pool isolation" href="/docs/engine" icon="box" tag="Infrastructure" description="Verifies the 1:1 pool wiring and the live credential-level isolation between databases." meta="regression" />
    <DocCard title="Blind pentest" href="/docs/testing/blind-pentest" icon="target" tag="External view" description="Confirms the system detects and classifies activity with no insider knowledge of the routing logic." meta="protocol" />
    <DocCard title="Diagnostics" href="#secret" icon="lock" tag="Gated" description="Route and score headers are only available with the internal test secret, so tests get evidence without exposing an oracle." meta="fail closed" />
  </CardGrid>

